- *I-1* (#"SA-9 check_review_independence.py exit 1, one problem"): #"A SCHEMA DEFECT, NOT AN INDEPENDENCE FAILURE, conditional on CC-4. The seven entries at indices 12, 13, 17, 39, 47, 48 and 49 of the 8aff64 sources_read each contain an unquoted ': ' and parse as one-key mappings. This composer read each entry; they name: EXP-MONO-0e6e8f raw-result.json (by key), EXP-MONO-815525 run_census.py (lines 47-209), TASK-20260930-40470a s4_construction/computations.json (by key), templates/research-records.md (lines 675-789), agents/coordinator.md (lines 178-247), docs/claims-and-verification.md (lines 104-170) and EXP-MONO-815525 red-team-report.yaml (lines 256-300). None is a sibling artifact, the prior-holding decision or an excluded path. The checker also SKIPS non-string entries in its sibling test (tools/check_review_independence.py lines 953-966, `continue` on non-str), so its clean pass on the other entries does not cover these seven. CC-4 closes that gap mechanically on a normalized scratch copy. The committed file is not edited (SA-7; records immutable)."
- *I-2* (#"TASK-20261017-ccd10c read .claude/agents/validator.md and docs/inventor-protocol.md, outside its whitelist"): #"A DISCLOSED READ-SCOPE DEVIATION (RB-9), CAUSED BY THE CARD, WITH NO EFFECT ON BLINDNESS. Neither path is under any blind_from entry (the list names coordination/, ledger/, knowledge/, experiments/, analysis/ and research/ paths; docs/ and .claude/ are not in it), so RA-C6's not-independent clause is not triggered and the checker correctly raised nothing for ccd10c. Neither file contains the quantities: this composer's search of each for monodromy, Semaev, V_4 and summation found no match (and S_4 none in validator.md). The binding text the re-deriver had to read (.claude/agents/validator-breakthrough.md lines 27-32) directs the reader to both files, and the card's whitelist omitted them: a card-design defect of the opening Coordinator session, not a reviewer defect. Lesson LS-4."
- *I-3* (#"TASK-20261017-8aff64 read four decision ranges outside its inputs for Q-OI"): #"A DISCLOSED READ-SCOPE EXCESS, PURPOSE-BOUND, WITH NO EFFECT ON COMPOSITION. DEC-20260930-3a0b7b lines 184-194, DEC-20260904-0f525b lines 40-66, DEC-20260904-4eb323 lines 184-192 and DEC-20260904-8c2580 lines 118-156 are grep-located single ranges, declared by path and line. None is an excluded path (the excluded set is DEC-20261017-12e0f4, the ccd10c directory and records, EXP-MONO-4b50b6/ and BATCH-003/), none is a sibling artifact, and none holds the coordinator prior. This composer read DEC-20260904-8c2580 lines 118-156, DEC-20260802-a51c82 N-3 and DEC-20260810-2f86db N-3 (which carries the a51c82 N-3 repairs forward and adds \"No new census of any statistic may be dispatched before these are carried\") and finds the reviewer's quotations accurate. The grep -l listing that printed three file NAMES under the excluded BATCH-003/ path, with no content, is name-level exposure only; 8aff64 is not a blind re-deriver and BATCH-003 is kept closed for later blind rounds, of which this goal now has none. Lesson LS-6."
- *I-4* (#"the mutual-blindness measure (holding folder) and the shared scratchpad"): #"ACCEPTED AS A CUSTODY MEASURE OUTSIDE THE PLAN (PD-1); MUTUAL BLINDNESS OF 8aff64 FROM RB RESTS ON ATTESTATION, CORROBORATED; RB's BLINDNESS FROM 8aff64 IS STRUCTURAL. (a) Custody: the moved files were restored with identical sha256 (runtime receipt) and equal the release digests (SA-4), so no byte changed. (b) Direction RB -> RA: ccd10c ran and was released before 8aff64 was claimed, so it could not see 8aff64's output. (c) Direction RA -> RB: the measure kept the sibling's output out of the working tree, and 8aff64 reports that ccd10c's directory did not exist in its checkout. But the ccd10c runtime receipt also discloses that all its scripts were written and run in the shared session scratchpad, and 8aff64 attests that it listed foreign scratchpad directories (blind/, rb/, held/, ...) by name once and never opened them. That residual exposure cannot be checked after the fact; it rests on 8aff64's attestation. It is corroborated by method divergence: different curves and primes (8aff64 p = 53, 59, 101, 1009, 10007, 10009; ccd10c p = 101, 103, 997, 1009, 1013, 1019, sharing only the (101, 2, 3) curve), different S_5 constructions (per-fibre 12-point interpolation of Res_X(S_4, S_3) against full-grid interpolation of the formal Sylvester determinant), different exact-count methods (enumeration of the degenerate locus against closed-form class counts), and different S_4 term counts (439 monomials in x with Z[a,b] coefficients against 540 terms; a counting-convention difference, not reconciled here, not a Q1-Q4 quantity and relied on by neither). Composition consequence: RB is independent of both the producer and 8aff64; RA-1 to RA-3 count as a second re-derivation independent of RB by attestation and divergence, not by construction. Lesson LS-3."
